From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Henrik Klee <henrik@goat-code.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 21:35:03 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] drm/imagination: apple: Split chip specifics from the Apple
 firmware path

The A9's GPU runs the same family of Apple firmware as the A10's: work
rings and completion stamps per engine, an event ring, Fender's power
state. What differs is the processor the firmware runs on (the A10's is
an RTKit coprocessor), how it is booted and rung, and the layout of the
memory it shares with the host, commands included.

Put that behind struct pvr_apple_chip, chosen by the compatible, and
move the A10's side to pvr_apple_t8010.c: RTKit, the firmware window,
the init handshake, the doorbell, the job writers and the translation of
the geometry and fragment commands into them. pvr_apple.c keeps what the
chips share: submission and its ordering, fences and completion, events,
Fender power and performance states, runtime PM, sleep and recovery. It
reaches the firmware's memory through offsets the chip sets
(struct pvr_apple_layout) and takes the command stream definitions from
the chip.

No change for the A10: the same register writes and firmware messages in
the same order. Two things move within host-only code: at removal and
on a failed probe the completion pollers are cancelled after the run bit
is cleared instead of just before it (as runtime and system suspend
always did), and a firmware start resets the sequence numbers before
clearing the firmware's memory instead of after.

Assisted-by: LLM
